WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.439
Our friend called us

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.319
and said that the war had begun.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:16.920
When Russia attacked Ukraine on 24 February 2022,

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.400
the European Parliament and the EU

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.439
immediately condemned the aggression.

00:00:21.439 --> 00:00:24.720
Europe took action to support Ukraine.

00:00:26.639 --> 00:00:29.759
We understood that staying in Kyiv was very dangerous.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.879
As Russia's aggression grew bolder

00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:33.600
and the destruction increased,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.720
Parliament backed round after round

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.759
of economic sanctions on Putin and his enablers.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.720
We drove for 27 hours without stopping,

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.680
we didn't sleep, we didn't eat, nothing.

00:00:46.759 --> 00:00:49.959
When millions of people fled the rockets and shells,

00:00:49.959 --> 00:00:52.039
Europeans opened their doors

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:55.959
and the EU granted refugees unprecedented protection.

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:01.519
Of course, we are extremely grateful to European countries

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:03.839
that came together at the start of the war

00:01:03.839 --> 00:01:07.280
and took in a huge number of Ukrainian refugees.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:18.280
Poland helps a lot with clothes, food and medicines.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.039
They don't just bring help,

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:23.360
they always ask what people need.

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:26.600
As Russia plunged Ukraine into darkness

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.000
by attacking power supplies and civilian infrastructure,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.079
as winter began to bite,

00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:34.759
Parliament sent Generators of Hope.

00:01:36.159 --> 00:01:39.239
I am worried about my relatives who stayed in Ukraine.

00:01:39.239 --> 00:01:41.759
They live in fear of renewed attacks.

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:45.600
There are so many problems with power and food supplies.

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:49.800
When Russia committed war crimes,

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.439
Parliament declared it a state sponsor of terrorism.

00:01:53.439 --> 00:01:55.280
When Ukraine’s economy buckled,

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.200
Parliament backed suspending import duties

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.959
and voted for €18 billion of support for Ukraine in 2023.

00:02:03.959 --> 00:02:07.119
As Ukrainians fought for their freedom and democracy,

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:08.800
Parliament called for more weapons

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.720
and assistance for the country's military.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.400
When Russia tried to isolate Ukraine,

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.759
Parliament backed granting it EU-candidate status,

00:02:18.759 --> 00:02:22.039
paving the way to join the European Union.

00:02:22.039 --> 00:02:26.439
Ukraine's future is in the European Union. Slava Ukraini!

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.680
I believe that Ukraine is a European country

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:41.639
and our mindset is not very different.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.800
Slava Ukraini!

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.519
Glory to the heroes!

00:02:56.479 --> 00:02:58.319
We were with you then,

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:00.039
we are with you now,

00:03:00.039 --> 00:03:03.600
we will be with you for as long as it takes.

